 ## Outputs
 
-- **TRIG** - A 10 V pulse each time the playhead lands on a hit. It is 1 ms long by default; **Trigger length** in the right-click menu goes up to 200 ms. Every hit gets its own rising edge: if a new hit lands while the previous pulse is still high, the output drops to 0 V for one sample first, so a fast clock never merges two hits into one long pulse. It is Euclid's only output: for a sustained gate, run TRIG into an envelope or a gate-length utility.
+- **TRIG** - A 10 V pulse each time the playhead lands on a hit. It is 1 ms long by default; **Trigger length** in the right-click menu goes up to 200 ms. Every hit gets its own rising edge: if a new hit lands while the previous pulse is still high, the output drops to 0 V for one sample first, so a fast clock never merges two hits into one long pulse. There is no gate output: for a sustained gate, run TRIG into an envelope or a gate-length utility.
+- **ACCENT** - A 10 V pulse on every Nth hit, where N is the **ACCENT** knob; at 0 the jack stays at 0 V. It fires together with TRIG on that hit and is exactly as long, set by the same **Trigger length**, and like TRIG it gives every accent its own rising edge. Patch it into a drum's accent input, or into a second voice to double every fourth hit with a crash.
 
 ## Reset and the First Step
 
